# ROCKNIX ABL for the Pocket MICRO 2

The ROCKNIX ABL for SM8250 that this MicroOS install ships, taken from the ROCKNIX/abl release at build time and
listed in `manifest`.

This folder is the first install. A device still in stock Android runs the vendor ABL, which does not boot `\KERNEL`,
so both slots are written from Android before MicroOS ever starts. Once MicroOS runs, `microos-abl update` writes a
later ROCKNIX release from Linux, with the same backup and readback.

Copy this folder from the card to the root of Android internal storage. The card's ESP can be mounted read only, and
the backups are written here. Then run these from a root shell. They write `/dev/block/by-name/abl_a` and `abl_b`.

## Back up both slots

    sh backup_abl.sh

Writes `abl-<sha256>.img` and its `.sha256` for each slot in this folder. The image is the whole partition, and the
partition is hashed again after the file.

## Write both slots

    sh flash_abl.sh

Checks the elf against its `.sha256`, both slots against a backup in this folder, and each slot's `order` in
`releases.tsv`: a slot at or above the payload's order is refused. A slot that is not in `releases.tsv` is written with
a warning. The inactive slot goes first from `ro.boot.slot_suffix`, then the active one, and each is read back.

## Restore one slot

    sh restore_backup_abl.sh a abl-<sha256>.img

## Files

`abl_signed-SM8250.elf` and `.sha256`: the bootloader. `releases.tsv`: `order version soc length sha256`, one row per
ROCKNIX ABL, a higher `order` is newer. `manifest`: what this MicroOS install ships.

## Overrides

`ABL_BLOCK_DIR` (`/dev/block/by-name`), `ABL_BACKUP` and `ABL_PAYLOAD` (this folder).
